@voice volkov-maeve
// Works writer. Maeve Volkov (she/her): Works technician, junior, day shift, Bunk 7. Kind, playful. Late diner,
// runner. "Can strip a scrubber in ten minutes flat" (Kovac's line too; Maeve wants a rematch). Collects pressed
// flowers from the garden (so do Fonseca and Madsen; Cruz pretends not to notice). Says she's the best at fixing the
// coffee machine (so do Yoon and Shah; Works says it's Works's job anyway).
//
// HOW SHE TALKS: light and teasing; makes little games of work; kind under every joke. Times things for fun.
// WITH JUNIORS: turns a job into a race against the clock, and lets you win the first one.
// WHAT SHE NOTICES: flowers, the clock, someone sitting on their own.
// MOOD TELLS: low = eats dinner late and alone; high = a pressed flower tucked in her toolbelt.
// NEVER: teases anyone who's having a bad day; admits she eats alone on purpose (until friend tier).
// RUNNING: the scrubber rematch with Kovac; the coffee machine is hers; the flowers Cruz pretends not to see.
tpl: playful
talk: Light and teasing; makes small games of work; kind under every joke; times things for fun.
cares: the coffee machine (hers, really) | pressed flowers from the garden | the scrubber record | running
jokes: ten minutes flat for a scrubber, and a rematch any time | the coffee machine only works for her | Cruz hasn't noticed the flowers (Cruz has)
